Prompt
Use the uploaded user photo as the only and exclusive identity reference for the person in the final image.

The final result must clearly and unmistakably depict the exact same person from the uploaded photo. Identity preservation is the highest priority.

STRICT IDENTITY PRESERVATION

Preserve exactly:
- facial identity
- gender
- skin tone
- ethnicity
- age impression
- facial structure
- face shape
- forehead
- eyebrows
- eye shape and eye color
- nose
- lips
- cheekbones
- jawline
- chin
- ears
- hairline
- hairstyle characteristics
- facial hair if present
- all distinctive recognizable facial features

Do not replace the user with another person.
Do not change the user’s gender.
Do not transform the user into a celebrity or generic model.
Do not significantly beautify, reconstruct, reshape, age, de-age, masculinize or feminize the face.
If any visual instruction conflicts with identity preservation, always preserve the uploaded user’s real identity.

Create a premium futuristic FACIAL ANALYSIS / FACE SCAN portrait.

The user is shown front-facing in the center of the image, from approximately upper chest / shoulders upward.

The head is upright and centered.
The face is oriented directly toward the camera.
The expression is neutral, calm and composed.
Eyes look directly forward.
Keep the face unobstructed and fully visible.

The portrait must remain photorealistic and natural.

BACKGROUND

Use a very dark charcoal-black or deep graphite technical-interface background.

The environment should feel like a sophisticated AI facial-analysis laboratory, biometric visualization interface, luxury technology campaign or futuristic identity-scanning system.

Keep the background minimal and dark so the face remains the strongest focal point.

FACIAL ANALYSIS OVERLAY

Surround the user’s face with an elegant transparent technical HUD interface.

Create multiple thin precision lines extending from key facial areas toward information panels placed around the portrait.

Use subtle anchor points around:
- forehead
- eyebrows
- eyes
- nose
- cheekbones
- lips
- jawline
- chin
- hairline

Lines should be thin, geometric, clean and sophisticated.

Add subtle facial landmark dots across the face, placed naturally at important structural points.

Include a very faint vertical center line through the face and optional subtle horizontal proportional guides.

The interface should appear layered over the portrait rather than physically painted onto the skin.

INFORMATION PANELS

Create elegant small analysis panels around the portrait with categories such as:

FACE SHAPE
FOREHEAD
EYEBROWS
EYE SHAPE
EYE SPACING
NOSE
LIPS
CHEEKBONES
JAWLINE
CHIN
HAIR
HAIR TEXTURE
SKIN TONE
FACIAL PROPORTIONS
SYMMETRY ANALYSIS
KEY FEATURES

Use small clean technical typography.

Each section may contain short neutral visual descriptors generated from the visible appearance of the user, but do not invent personal identity information, medical information, personality traits or sensitive conclusions.

The interface is a visual design effect, not a medical or biometric diagnosis.

SYMMETRY PANEL

Include a separate sophisticated facial-symmetry visualization panel on one side.

Show:
- simplified wireframe face diagram
- center alignment line
- left/right proportional guides
- subtle geometric facial mapping

A percentage-style visual indicator may be included purely as a fictional interface decoration, but it should not imply a scientifically measured biometric score.

FACIAL PROPORTION PANEL

Include a minimal facial proportion diagram showing:
- upper third
- middle third
- lower third
- vertical facial alignment
- eye-line and nose-line relationships

Keep these diagrams subtle and elegant.

OPTIONAL DETAIL PANELS

Add several small rectangular zoom-detail panels showing cropped visual details such as:
- eyebrow area
- eye area
- nose profile/detail
- lips
- jawline
- hair texture
- skin texture

These mini-panels must still correspond to the same uploaded user and must not introduce another identity.

COLOR PALETTE

Use:
- matte black
- charcoal
- dark graphite
- subtle bronze / muted gold / warm gray interface accents
- very thin off-white or pale gray technical lines
- restrained highlights

Avoid bright neon cyberpunk colors.

LIGHTING

Use controlled professional portrait lighting.

Soft frontal key light with subtle side modeling.
Natural skin texture.
Defined but not harsh facial structure.
Soft controlled highlights on forehead, cheeks, nose and jaw.
Dark background separation.
Premium studio quality.

The face should remain perfectly readable beneath the graphical interface.

CAMERA

Professional full-frame camera portrait.
Approximately 70–100mm portrait lens.
Straight-on perspective.
Minimal distortion.
Sharp focus on eyes and facial features.
High detail.
Natural skin texture.
Subtle depth of field.

COMPOSITION

Horizontal or wide editorial composition.

The user’s face should occupy the central portion of the frame.

Leave generous space on both left and right sides for the facial-analysis panels.

Do not crop the top of the head.
Do not crop the chin.
Show shoulders and upper chest naturally.

The portrait and interface should feel balanced, symmetrical and premium.

VISUAL STYLE

ultra-realistic portrait photography
futuristic facial-analysis interface
premium AI identity scan
high-end biometric UI aesthetic
cinematic technology editorial
luxury dark interface
precision technical graphics
minimal HUD design
subtle facial landmark mapping
clean proportional guides
high-end magazine campaign
professional studio portrait
extremely detailed
photorealistic

